{"type":"data","nodes":[null,null,{"type":"data","data":[{"code":1,"requestedAs":1,"title":2,"credits":3,"creditsPending":4,"subject":5,"listings":6,"offered":13,"eligibleYears":15,"description":17,"prerequisites":18,"unlocks":25,"equivalents":26,"lecturers":27,"terms":32,"programmes":35,"batches":53},"BIOS235","Animal Behaviour",4,false,"biology",[7,9],{"subject":5,"href":8,"code":1},"/programmes/biology",{"subject":10,"href":11,"code":12},"environmental studies","/programmes/environmental-studies","ENVS236",[14],1,[16,3],3,"This course will begin with an overview of animal behaviour and how it has integrated concepts from many disciplines to advance the field. Next, animal behaviour will be studied from an evolutionary perspective before understanding the bases for the variation in behaviours within and among individuals, populations, and species. With these concepts in mind, a range of behaviours will be examined using case studies. Finally, more complex behaviours related to social interactions among animals will be considered.",[19,22],{"code":20,"title":21,"credits":3},"BIOS201","Life at Different Scales",{"code":23,"title":24,"credits":3},"BIOS224","Evolution",[],[],[28],{"id":29,"name":30,"title":31},"shivani-jadeja","Shivani Jadeja","Assistant Professor, Biological Sciences",[33,34],"2026 T1","2024 T1",[36,48],{"subject":5,"slug":5,"required":37,"choice":38,"elective":39},[],[],[40,41,42,43,44,45,46,47],"4-year major","4-year double major","3-year major","3-year double major","4-year minor","3-year minor","concentration (4-year)","concentration (3-year)",{"subject":10,"slug":49,"required":50,"choice":51,"elective":52},"environmental-studies",[],[],[40,41,42,43,44,45,46,47],"2024–2026"],"uses":{"params":["code"]}}]}
